---
description: Path geometry for chrome icons; Noto Sans UI text OK; no fluent Button
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Unicode chrome icons (mandatory)

Windows fonts and bundled Noto Sans **lack** many symbol glyphs. Unicode
chrome icons (`✎`, `×`, `✕`, `✓`, `❐`, `─`, `▾`, `▸`, `›`, `●`, `↑`, `↓`,
`↩`, `＋`, `－`, …) render as **tofu** (empty boxes / two vertical rectangles).

This has already bitten caption buttons, Projects edit/delete, **and**
TERMINALS/FILES section chevrons. A narrow “grep only ✎×✓” pass is **not**
enough — any symbol used as an icon must be Path.

Fluent `Button` from `std-widgets.slint` also looks foreign next to Theme
chrome. Prefer `AppButton`.

## Icons

- Chrome actions MUST use **Path geometry** (`SectionDot`,
  `TerminalRowIcon`, `CaptionButton`, or an inline `Path` with a fixed
  viewbox). Status / section markers MUST be a small `Rectangle` with
  `border-radius` (colored disc) — never Unicode `●` / `▾` / `▸`.
  TERMINALS markers use `Theme.accent`; FILES use `Theme.include`.
- NEVER put symbol glyphs in `Text { text: "…" }` for buttons, row actions,
  section collapse, menu chevrons, find arrows, or filter chip signs.
- ASCII `+` / `-` in labels is OK (e.g. `"+ Include"`). Prose punctuation
  (`—`, `…`) in sentences is OK.

## Text labels and buttons

- Dialog / form actions MUST use **`AppButton`** (`form-dialogs.slint`) or
  another Theme + `TouchArea` control — never `import { Button } from
  "std-widgets.slint"`.
- Chrome text (menus, sidebar, tabs, dialogs, AppButton) uses bundled
  **Noto Sans** (proportional) via Window `default-font-family: "Noto Sans"`
  and `assets/NotoSans-Regular.ttf` / `NotoSans-Bold.ttf` (OFL).
- NEVER force a **mono** face on chrome (`Noto Sans Mono`, Cascadia Mono/Code,
  Consolas). Mono is for the viewport bitmap only (separate).

## Allowed fluent leftovers

- `Palette` / `SpinBox` may remain until a Theme replacement exists.
- Do **not** add new fluent `Button`, `LineEdit`, or Unicode icon `Text`.

## Agent obligations

- After chrome icon/button/font changes: rebuild
  `cargo build --profile release-dev -p noviewlog-slint` (Windows:
  `.\scripts\run-slint-windows.ps1` or MSVC env + same cargo).
- Do **not** rely on a hand-picked glyph grep. Run:

```
cargo test -p noviewlog-slint --test chrome_icon_wiring
cargo test -p noviewlog-slint --test inline_rename_wiring
```

  `chrome_icon_wiring` fails if any `ui/*.slint` `text: "…"` still contains
  banned icon codepoints (including `▾`/`▸`).
